{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1094449-gm-advice-handling-human-souls","id":1094449,"title":"GM advice handling human souls","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-19T00:55:37-07:00","id":1094449,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> GM advice handling human souls","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Hello guys,</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I will GM in the near future M20 xover oWoD - don't say anything, it works for us.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">It's an ongoing </span></span>chronicle <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">for maybe 10 years in which we change the GM every 3-7 sessions.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I have to GM after the &quot;special&quot; GM in our group made some decisions.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Now I have a fairly new M20 player with two human souls.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">How do I/you handle souls in M20? Spirit? Mind? Both?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The player is pretty dedicated to &quot;save&quot; the other soul and want essentially change his whole concept with skilling spirit and/or mind (from 0) to 4? 5? to get it out of his body.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">He knows that would take several years of playing this character and put every little xp in this project.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Now I want to support this as far as I can without giving him &quot;the staff of soul exchange&quot;.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">So first:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What IS the human soul (for you) in M20 and how do I manipulate it? Is it just the consciousness and manipulated by the mind sphere? Or is it something else? Something divine maybe and I need the spirit sphere?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">In Mage Rev. you needed Life 5, Mind 5, Spirit 5 to create a -whole- human being. Do you think this is still valid?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The M20-How-To does in the necromany section also say spirit could be needed to find and &quot;summon&quot; souls. But in my case the soul is there. It doesn't need to be summon from the afterlife and/or an umbra realm.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">So how do I or would you handle this situation?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I would be also grateful for every other ideas to support the player with.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">cheers<br /> lastlostboy</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12609,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","user":"lastlostboy","date":". 05-19-2017, 03:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","name":"lastlostboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T02:24:00-07:00","id":1094466,"title":"","content":"The human soul is what becomes a Wraith after the human dies, so that could be a good place to start. Spirit can manipulate it.<br /> <br /> If your Mage believes that the soul is what we refer to when talking about consciousness then perhaps Mind is more appropriate. In which case the Afterwotlds of the astral realm is where this Mage would focus their attention rather than the shadowlands.<br /> <br /> Summoning a soul from the afterlife is necromancy, no two ways about it.<br /> <br /> If you want to sever a living person's soul from their body, then that would be a ritual not unlike gilgul. I'd require master of spirit and life to attempt it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T05:10:05-07:00","id":1094490,"title":"","content":"The soul is the Avatar. As demonstrated by the soulless flaw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T08:02:24-07:00","id":1094557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1094449-gm-advice-handling-human-souls?p=1094490#post1094490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The soul is the Avatar. As demonstrated by the soulless flaw.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry but... - no.<br /> Do you really want to say only awakend mages do have souls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","name":"lastlostboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T08:32:41-07:00","id":1094567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lastlostboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1094449-gm-advice-handling-human-souls#post1094449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do I/you handle souls in M20? Spirit? Mind? Both?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage does not have a strong technical definition of soul, because it is obligated to make <i>atman </i>and <i>anatman </i>both potentially viable viewpoints. Wraiths are often called &quot;souls&quot;, in the sense that they are soulforged and such, but it's not a given that a wraith &quot;is&quot; all of the person they once were. Likewise, the Avatar is occasionally called a soul, or a fragment of Prime embedded in the soul, blah blah blah.<br /> <br /> So, getting away from the inexact jargon: Your player's character has a separate, independent mind, with volition, in their body. In Mage Sphere terms, making a full and complete person requires Life (for the body), Mind (for the mind), and Spirit (for volition/self-direction). Once created, though, it generally does not require Spirit to move the willful personality around (otherwise astral projection wouldn't work.)<br /> <br /> If you were feeling polite, then, it will only take Mind (5) to get the other occupant out of the body and invest them into a new one (which would take just Life[/Prime] to make.)<br /> <br /> In M20, investing a Mind into a body requires Life 4...for some reason... so the character might not be able to get away with having someone else make the body for them.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to make it more difficult, you could say that they were entangled on some spiritual/Avatar level, in which case you'd also need Spirit, probably around Spirit 4, to split them. Spirit 4 can manually push spiritual matter around, which sounds like what you'd need.<br /> <br /> So!<br /> <br /> <b>Easy Mode: </b>Mind 5 to transfer consciousness, need to ask someone with Life 5 to make a body for you.<br /> <b>M20 Mode: </b>Mind 5/Life 4 to transfer consciousness (also probably conjunctional Prime 2 and Spirit 2 if you read HDYDT), need to ask someone with Life 5 to make a body<br /> <b>Complicated Mode: </b>Mind 5 to transfer the consciousness, Spirit 4 to split the twins, need to ask someone to make a body, etc.<br /> <br /> That's a lot of Master and Adept Spheres, though. I think it would be better for a play group to instead have the character cultivate Spirit and Mind up to ~3-ish and conduct interviews with spirits and with their own &quot;other self&quot;, and when they have a good handle on the nature of their condition, give them a quest into the Umbra to have a powerful umbrood or other being do the split for them.<br /> <br /> That way you get more character scenes (instead of &quot;rolling Arete&quot; scenes) and you have a method that other players can participate in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T08:48:39-07:00","id":1094572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lastlostboy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry but... - no.<br /> Do you really want to say only awakend mages do have souls?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but, in Mage, all living humans have Avatars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-19-2017, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T10:40:36-07:00","id":1094614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1094449-gm-advice-handling-human-souls?p=1094567#post1094567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage does not have a strong technical definition of soul, because it is obligated to make <i>atman </i>and <i>anatman </i>both potentially viable viewpoints. Wraiths are often called &quot;souls&quot;, in the sense that they are soulforged and such, but it's not a given that a wraith &quot;is&quot; all of the person they once were. Likewise, the Avatar is occasionally called a soul, or a fragment of Prime embedded in the soul, blah blah blah.<br /> <br /> So, getting away from the inexact jargon: Your player's character has a separate, independent mind, with volition, in their body. In Mage Sphere terms, making a full and complete person requires Life (for the body), Mind (for the mind), and Spirit (for volition/self-direction). Once created, though, it generally does not require Spirit to move the willful personality around (otherwise astral projection wouldn't work.)<br /> <br /> If you were feeling polite, then, it will only take Mind (5) to get the other occupant out of the body and invest them into a new one (which would take just Life[/Prime] to make.)<br /> <br /> In M20, investing a Mind into a body requires Life 4...for some reason... so the character might not be able to get away with having someone else make the body for them.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to make it more difficult, you could say that they were entangled on some spiritual/Avatar level, in which case you'd also need Spirit, probably around Spirit 4, to split them. Spirit 4 can manually push spiritual matter around, which sounds like what you'd need.<br /> <br /> So!<br /> <br /> <b>Easy Mode: </b>Mind 5 to transfer consciousness, need to ask someone with Life 5 to make a body for you.<br /> <b>M20 Mode: </b>Mind 5/Life 4 to transfer consciousness (also probably conjunctional Prime 2 and Spirit 2 if you read HDYDT), need to ask someone with Life 5 to make a body<br /> <b>Complicated Mode: </b>Mind 5 to transfer the consciousness, Spirit 4 to split the twins, need to ask someone to make a body, etc.<br /> <br /> That's a lot of Master and Adept Spheres, though. I think it would be better for a play group to instead have the character cultivate Spirit and Mind up to ~3-ish and conduct interviews with spirits and with their own &quot;other self&quot;, and when they have a good handle on the nature of their condition, give them a quest into the Umbra to have a powerful umbrood or other being do the split for them.<br /> <br /> That way you get more character scenes (instead of &quot;rolling Arete&quot; scenes) and you have a method that other players can participate in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that helps a lot.<br /> My character is a mind mage and although I would never use them as a GM to settle such things he might help in the future with a possible ritual.<br /> For now I keep a Mind 5 / Spirit X solution in... mind. (Sorry.)<br /> <br /> The next hard part: the &quot;body&quot;.<br /> The player wants - as I said, we don't really have outright plans for this &quot;situation&quot;, we just want to see what is possible and what is not - to bind the soul in his node/sanctum. Don't look at me like this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I as a GM hate to say something is impossible especially in Mage. I'm totally fine with needing pattern spheres for this kind of task but what if I want to bind something in a <i>place</i>? I don't need correspondence right? Is it even possible or would I need matter to bind it in the <i>ground</i> of the place? Or spirit to bind it in the ethereal pattern of the place?<br /> Yes I said the chronicle has already a 10 years lifespan but for the most time it was a Fallen/Ananasi/Bastet pairing so please excuse my Mage noob questions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I've read HDYDT when it came out. I really like the idea for inspiration and so on but there were a few things outright BS and I use it more as a... guideline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1094449-gm-advice-handling-human-souls?p=1094572#post1094572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, but, in Mage, all living humans have Avatars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. But I don't only have the Mage point of view.<br /> We like our Fera and Fallen with souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12609,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","user":"lastlostboy","date":". 05-19-2017, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","name":"lastlostboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T11:08:01-07:00","id":1094621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I as a GM hate to say something is impossible especially in Mage. I'm totally fine with needing pattern spheres for this kind of task but what if I want to bind something in a <i>place</i>? I don't need correspondence right? Is it even possible or would I need matter to bind it in the <i>ground</i> of the place? Or spirit to bind it in the ethereal pattern of the place? </div> </div> </div>If you don't think the soul will go away, you just need to place it &quot;there&quot;. Personally, I think the disembodied soul it's going to go wherever souls go when the body die. To bind it to a place you will need, likely, Spirit (possibly Correspondence too, like when capturing spirits or wraiths in HDYDT inside a Ward...that can also be used to capture Mages that used Mind to leave their bodies and now're conveniently ephemeral...I would say that Demons probably can be &quot;sealed&quot; that way too). I don't think that it's necessary to bind the soul to the soil...but if you want, it may take away the Correspondence requirement and replace it with Matter, or maybe it will suffice with Spirit alone (you don't need Matter to craft a Fetish).<br /> It could be argued that Spirit 4 alone can do the &quot;bind a soul to a place&quot; too, without Correspondence, saying that Spirit does all the Binding, while Correspondence it's just to Ward (to impede the spirit to use it's powers on the outside, but we don't need that). I think I like this approach better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-19-2017, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}